# Vite `--mode desktop` env — loaded on top of .env for the Tauri desktop build ONLY.
#
# Committed on purpose: it holds no secrets, and it is what makes `isDesktop` true at build
# time (src/lib/platform.ts). Vite inlines it, so the desktop branches are constant-folded and
# the browser bundle never carries them.
#
# For a RELEASE build against the deployed backend, put the production URLs in a gitignored
# .env.desktop.local next to this file. CI release builds read the same three from the
# repository's Actions variables instead (see docs/desktop.md, Releasing).
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.tendto.work
#   VITE_AUTH_URL=https://auth.tendto.work
#   VITE_POWERSYNC_URL=https://sync.tendto.work
#
# Do NOT create .env.desktop.local on a dev machine you also run `make desktop` on: Vite loads it
# for dev as well as for builds, so the dev shell would quietly talk to production.
VITE_PLATFORM=desktop
